      "text": "Midlothian grew around a milk stop on the Rock Island Railroad before becoming a village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofmidlothian.net/99/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name comes from an ancient Scottish borough and was adopted after a local country club’s popularity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofmidlothian.net/99/History",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original Midlothian train station was built near the village’s boundaries and later became part of downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midlothian%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Midlothian’s present Village Hall, built in 1949, sits at 148th and Pulaski.",
